        "Musharakah agreements may allow the bank to convert outstanding investment into ordinary shares, require clearance before dividends, and provide adjudication or review committees; banks need stronger appraisal and monitoring.",
        "Project finance: Mudarabah if the financier funds all; Musharakah if both invest; combination if one party manages.",
        "Running Musharakah flow: (1) running Musharakah account opened; (2) sale proceeds credited; (3) investing and long-term financing cash flows excluded; (4) clients categorised as seasonal, cyclical or continuous; (5) profit paid monthly/quarterly; (6) sharing based on computed operating profit for the limit period.",
        "Certificates (TFCs, PTCs) reduce moral hazard compared with direct Musharakah.",
        "Risks cited by banks: manipulated reporting, non-disclosure of profit, collateral only for negligence, allocation of personal expenses, guarantor independence, and unit-price fluctuation in DM.",
